1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,367
Day six. Bad air. Your lungs clamp
shut. Last puff. Nothing in the can.

2
00:00:04,867 --> 00:00:08,567
You drop to your knees between the
cots. The room starts to go gray.

3
00:00:09,067 --> 00:00:10,900
Out for four. In for two.

4
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,733
A hand on your back. Heavy. Hot.
Shaking.

5
00:00:14,233 --> 00:00:18,033
Out for four. In for two. Who taught
you to hold your breath, kid?

6
00:00:18,533 --> 00:00:19,000
Dad.

7
00:00:20,533 --> 00:00:27,067
I taught your sister that count when
she was six. You were the one who
needed it. You just wouldn't sit
still.

8
00:00:27,567 --> 00:00:33,133
He presses something into your hand.
An old inhaler. Two puffs. He saved it
for twenty years.

9
00:00:33,633 --> 00:00:35,667
Same lungs. Sorry about that.
